              Decentralised Governance Help Guide – Round Table, Votes, Objector's Bench, Audit Chain &amp; Simulator
            </h1>

            <p class="text-xl md:text-2xl text-center font-medium text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300 mb-10 leading-relaxed max-w-4xl">
              How the Traffic Torch Round Table turns every decision into a public, verifiable, reversible process — and how you can watch it happen in 30 seconds.
            </p>

            <div class="prose prose-lg prose-orange dark:prose-invert max-w-none mb-12">
              <p class="text-gray-800 dark:text-gray-200 leading-relaxed text-lg">
                The Traffic Torch <strong>Round Table</strong> is a live governance system running on the same site you're reading now. Every eligible user has equal voting authority. No admin table exists — by design. Every action is hash-chained and publically verifiable. Every decision is reversible. And every rule can be changed, but only by clearing the highest threshold on the site.
              </p>
              <p class="text-gray-800 dark:text-gray-200 leading-relaxed text-lg mt-6">
                This guide walks through the whole system: how proposals work, how votes are decided, how the block threshold protects minorities, how the Objector's Bench can pause but never block, how the audit chain proves nothing was altered, and how the simulator lets you watch the rules play out with no account, no vote, and no commitment.
              </p>
