            <!-- SECTION 1 -->
            <section id="what-is" class="mb-20 scroll-mt-24">
              <h2 class="text-4xl font-black text-center md:text-left text-gray-800 dark:text-gray-100 mb-10 bg-gradient-to-r from-orange-500 to-pink-600 bg-clip-text text-transparent">1. What is the Round Table?</h2>
              <div class="prose prose-lg prose-orange dark:prose-invert max-w-none">
                <p class="text-gray-800 dark:text-gray-200 leading-relaxed">The <strong>Round Table</strong> is the governance system that runs inside Traffic Torch. Every eligible user has one vote, and only one vote. No administrator can override a decision. No single account can edit the rules. Every proposal, comment, vote, objection, reconsideration, and execution is recorded on a public chain of hashes so that anyone can verify what actually happened.</p>
                <p class="text-gray-800 dark:text-gray-200 leading-relaxed mt-4">It runs on four principles:</p>
                <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 text-gray-800 dark:text-gray-200">
                  <li><strong>Equal authority.</strong> No privileged accounts. There is no admin table in the database. Every rule applies to every user identically, including the person who wrote the code.</li>
                  <li><strong>Tamper-evident.</strong> Every action produces a SHA-256 hash chained to the previous one. Modify any historic entry and the chain breaks — visibly.</li>
                  <li><strong>Minority-protected.</strong> The 25% block threshold means a 66% majority is necessary but not sufficient. Substantial opposition can stop any proposal.</li>
                  <li><strong>Reversible.</strong> Every resolution can be reopened within 30 days by 10% of eligible users. Nothing is permanent.</li>
                </ul>
                <p class="text-gray-800 dark:text-gray-200 leading-relaxed mt-6">Live URL: <a href="/community/round-table/" class="text-orange-600 dark:text-orange-400 hover:underline">/community/round-table/</a>. The constitution, founding document, and maintainer-powers document are all published alongside.</p>
                <p class="mt-8 text-center md:text-left"><a href="#table-of-contents" class="text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-400 hover:underline font-medium">← Return to TOC</a></p>
              </div>
            </section>

            <!-- SECTION 2 -->
            <section id="founding" class="mb-20 scroll-mt-24">
              <h2 class="text-4xl font-black text-center md:text-left text-gray-800 dark:text-gray-100 mb-10 bg-gradient-to-r from-orange-500 to-pink-600 bg-clip-text text-transparent">2. The founding documents</h2>
              <div class="prose prose-lg prose-orange dark:prose-invert max-w-none">
                <p class="text-gray-800 dark:text-gray-200 leading-relaxed">The system ships with three published documents and seven seed proposals that bootstrap the community from a blank database:</p>
                <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 text-gray-800 dark:text-gray-200">
                  <li><strong>Constitution.</strong> The rules. Amendments require a Meta proposal to clear 75% YES with under 25% NO. <a href="/community/round-table/constitution/" class="text-orange-600 dark:text-orange-400 hover:underline">/community/round-table/constitution/</a></li>
                  <li><strong>Founding Document.</strong> The origin story and the initial commitments: why the system exists, what it will never do, what early adopters agreed to. <a href="/community/round-table/founding/" class="text-orange-600 dark:text-orange-400 hover:underline">/community/round-table/founding/</a></li>
                  <li><strong>Maintainer Powers.</strong> A short, explicit list of what the code maintainer can and cannot do. Merging code, applying an already-approved config, running the R2 attachment purge — and nothing else. <a href="/community/round-table/maintainer-powers/" class="text-orange-600 dark:text-orange-400 hover:underline">/community/round-table/maintainer-powers/</a></li>
                </ul>
                <p class="text-gray-800 dark:text-gray-200 leading-relaxed mt-6">The seven seed proposals are pre-loaded when the governance tables are first created. They cover: ratifying the constitution, electing the first bench, enabling configurable pass thresholds, setting the initial consider window at 30 days, enabling reconsideration, publishing the maintainer powers, and bootstrapping the audit chain. All seven are visible in the feed from day one, so the community isn't starting from an empty board.</p>
                <p class="mt-8 text-center md:text-left"><a href="#table-of-contents" class="text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-400 hover:underline font-medium">← Return to TOC</a></p>
              </div>
            </section>

            <!-- SECTION 3 -->
            <section id="kinds" class="mb-20 scroll-mt-24">
              <h2 class="text-4xl font-black text-center md:text-left text-gray-800 dark:text-gray-100 mb-10 bg-gradient-to-r from-orange-500 to-pink-600 bg-clip-text text-transparent">3. Four kinds of proposal</h2>
              <div class="prose prose-lg prose-orange dark:prose-invert max-w-none">
                <p class="text-gray-800 dark:text-gray-200 leading-relaxed">Every proposal has a kind. The kind determines the pass threshold, the apply mechanism, and how the outcome affects the site:</p>
                <div class="not-prose overflow-x-auto mt-4">
                  <table class="w-full text-left border-collapse min-w-[600px] text-sm">
                    <thead>
                      <tr class="bg-gray-100 dark:bg-gray-800/80">
                        <th class="p-3 font-semibold text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300 border-b border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700">Kind</th>
                        <th class="p-3 font-semibold text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300 border-b border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700">Threshold</th>
                        <th class="p-3 font-semibold text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300 border-b border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700">What it changes</th>
                        <th class="p-3 font-semibold text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300 border-b border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700">On pass</th>
                      </tr>
                    </thead>
                    <tbody class="text-gray-800 dark:text-gray-200">
                      <tr><td class="p-3 border-b border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700"><strong>Advisory</strong></td><td class="p-3 border-b border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700">66%</td><td class="p-3 border-b border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700">Nothing structural. Records community signal.</td><td class="p-3 border-b border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700">Recorded only</td></tr>
                      <tr><td class="p-3 border-b border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700"><strong>Config</strong></td><td class="p-3 border-b border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700">66%</td><td class="p-3 border-b border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700">A config key: thresholds, quorum, block percentage.</td><td class="p-3 border-b border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700">Applied immediately</td></tr>
                      <tr><td class="p-3 border-b border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700"><strong>Meta</strong></td><td class="p-3 border-b border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700"><strong>75%</strong></td><td class="p-3 border-b border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700">The rules themselves — constitution, cadence, meta thresholds.</td><td class="p-3 border-b border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700">Applied after 72-hour delay</td></tr>
                      <tr><td class="p-3"><strong>Code</strong></td><td class="p-3">66%</td><td class="p-3">A code change, linked to a pull request.</td><td class="p-3">Records intent — human must merge PR</td></tr>
                    </tbody>
                  </table>
                </div>
                <p class="text-gray-800 dark:text-gray-200 leading-relaxed mt-6">The kind is set at creation and cannot be changed afterwards. If a proposal's body drifts from its kind, voters reject it on those grounds — and usually do.</p>
                <p class="mt-8 text-center md:text-left"><a href="#table-of-contents" class="text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-400 hover:underline font-medium">← Return to TOC</a></p>
              </div>
            </section>

            <!-- SECTION 4 -->
            <section id="phases" class="mb-20 scroll-mt-24">
              <h2 class="text-4xl font-black text-center md:text-left text-gray-800 dark:text-gray-100 mb-10 bg-gradient-to-r from-orange-500 to-pink-600 bg-clip-text text-transparent">4. Four phases</h2>
              <div class="prose prose-lg prose-orange dark:prose-invert max-w-none">
                <p class="text-gray-800 dark:text-gray-200 leading-relaxed">Every proposal moves through the same four phases in the same order. Each phase has a minimum duration that depends on the kind:</p>
                <div class="not-prose overflow-x-auto mt-4">
                  <table class="w-full text-left border-collapse min-w-[500px] text-sm">
                    <thead>
                      <tr class="bg-gray-100 dark:bg-gray-800/80">
                        <th class="p-3 font-semibold text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300 border-b border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700">Phase</th>
                        <th class="p-3 font-semibold text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300 border-b border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700">Duration</th>
                        <th class="p-3 font-semibold text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300 border-b border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700">What can happen</th>
                      </tr>
                    </thead>
                    <tbody class="text-gray-800 dark:text-gray-200">
                      <tr><td class="p-3 border-b border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700"><strong>Propose</strong></td><td class="p-3 border-b border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700">Instant</td><td class="p-3 border-b border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700">Author submits body, kind, category. Enters Discuss immediately.</td></tr>
                      <tr><td class="p-3 border-b border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700"><strong>Discuss</strong></td><td class="p-3 border-b border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700">Meta 30d · Config 14d · Code 14d · Advisory 7d</td><td class="p-3 border-b border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700">Comments, amendments by the author, bench discussion.</td></tr>
                      <tr><td class="p-3 border-b border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700"><strong>Vote</strong></td><td class="p-3 border-b border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700">5 days (all kinds)</td><td class="p-3 border-b border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700">Yes / No / Abstain. Bench objection can extend this by 72h.</td></tr>
                      <tr><td class="p-3"><strong>Execute</strong></td><td class="p-3">Per kind</td><td class="p-3">Config immediate · Meta 72h delayed · Code pending merge · Advisory recorded</td></tr>
                    </tbody>
                  </table>
                </div>
                <p class="text-gray-800 dark:text-gray-200 leading-relaxed mt-6">A proposal cannot skip a phase. The comment period must fully elapse before the author can open the vote. The vote must fully elapse before it can be closed. The execute step applies exactly what the voter was told would happen.</p>
                <p class="mt-8 text-center md:text-left"><a href="#table-of-contents" class="text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-400 hover:underline font-medium">← Return to TOC</a></p>
              </div>
            </section>

            <!-- SECTION 5 -->
            <section id="eligibility" class="mb-20 scroll-mt-24">
              <h2 class="text-4xl font-black text-center md:text-left text-gray-800 dark:text-gray-100 mb-10 bg-gradient-to-r from-orange-500 to-pink-600 bg-clip-text text-transparent">5. Eligibility — who can vote</h2>
              <div class="prose prose-lg prose-orange dark:prose-invert max-w-none">
                <p class="text-gray-800 dark:text-gray-200 leading-relaxed">The eligibility rule is one line of code and it is the exact rule the server enforces:</p>
                <pre class="bg-gray-100 dark:bg-black/40 rounded-lg p-4 text-sm overflow-x-auto text-gray-800 dark:text-gray-200"><code>eligible = account_age_days &gt;= 7
        &amp;&amp; (verified_at IS NOT NULL OR profile_public = 1)</code></pre>
                <p class="text-gray-800 dark:text-gray-200 leading-relaxed mt-4">That means: the account must be at least seven days old AND the user must have either verified their profile (email verification or higher) OR made their profile public.</p>
                <p class="text-gray-800 dark:text-gray-200 leading-relaxed mt-4">Why this rule?</p>
                <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 text-gray-800 dark:text-gray-200">
                  <li><strong>Seven days</strong> stops drive-by Sybil attacks. Creating a thousand accounts takes time, and seven days is long enough that farming them isn't worth the trouble for a single vote.</li>
                  <li><strong>Verification or public profile</strong> ensures the voter has actually engaged with the site — not just signed up and voted on a single proposal.</li>
                  <li><strong>No token gating, no purchase required.</strong> Governance does not require payment. Anyone can be eligible by simply being a genuine user for a week.</li>
                </ul>
                <p class="text-gray-800 dark:text-gray-200 leading-relaxed mt-6">The simulator reads this same rule. There is no divergence between what the server does, what the simulator shows, and what the constitution says.</p>
                <p class="mt-8 text-center md:text-left"><a href="#table-of-contents" class="text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-400 hover:underline font-medium">← Return to TOC</a></p>
              </div>
            </section>

            <!-- SECTION 6 -->
            <section id="vote" class="mb-20 scroll-mt-24">
              <h2 class="text-4xl font-black text-center md:text-left text-gray-800 dark:text-gray-100 mb-10 bg-gradient-to-r from-orange-500 to-pink-600 bg-clip-text text-transparent">6. The vote — quorum, thresholds, and the block</h2>
              <div class="prose prose-lg prose-orange dark:prose-invert max-w-none">
                <p class="text-gray-800 dark:text-gray-200 leading-relaxed">Three separate rules decide whether a vote passes. All three must be satisfied:</p>

                <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-800 dark:text-gray-200 mt-8">Quorum — enough votes to count</h3>
                <p class="text-gray-800 dark:text-gray-200 leading-relaxed">Quorum is the larger of <code class="text-orange-600 dark:text-orange-400">10 votes</code> or <code class="text-orange-600 dark:text-orange-400">20% of eligible users</code>. If the vote closes with fewer votes cast, the outcome is <strong>no_quorum</strong> regardless of the tally.</p>
                <p class="text-gray-800 dark:text-gray-200 leading-relaxed mt-4">Why the floor of 10? Small communities can't rely on 20%. At 40 eligible, 20% is 8 — too few to represent real community signal. The floor guarantees a minimum of 10 votes even in a tiny community.</p>

                <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-800 dark:text-gray-200 mt-8">Pass threshold — enough YES</h3>
                <p class="text-gray-800 dark:text-gray-200 leading-relaxed">Config, Code, and Advisory proposals need <strong>66% YES</strong>. Meta proposals need <strong>75% YES</strong>. The threshold is computed against <em>all votes cast</em>, including abstain. An abstain therefore dilutes YES and NO equally — it cannot be used as a stealth block.</p>

                <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-800 dark:text-gray-200 mt-8">The 25% block — enough NO to stop it</h3>
                <p class="text-gray-800 dark:text-gray-200 leading-relaxed">If NO is <strong>25% or more</strong> of votes cast, the proposal fails — regardless of YES. This rule is why 66% is necessary but not sufficient: a bare majority cannot override a substantial opposition.</p>

                <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-800 dark:text-gray-200 mt-8">A worked example</h3>
                <div class="not-prose overflow-x-auto mt-4">
                  <table class="w-full text-left border-collapse min-w-[500px] text-sm">
                    <thead>
                      <tr class="bg-gray-100 dark:bg-gray-800/80">
                        <th class="p-3 font-semibold text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300 border-b border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700">Case</th>
                        <th class="p-3 font-semibold text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300 border-b border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700">YES</th>
                        <th class="p-3 font-semibold text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300 border-b border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700">NO</th>
                        <th class="p-3 font-semibold text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300 border-b border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700">Abstain</th>
                        <th class="p-3 font-semibold text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300 border-b border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700">Outcome</th>
                      </tr>
                    </thead>
                    <tbody class="text-gray-800 dark:text-gray-200">
                      <tr><td class="p-3 border-b border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700">Clean pass</td><td class="p-3 border-b border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700">66</td><td class="p-3 border-b border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700">24</td><td class="p-3 border-b border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700">10</td><td class="p-3 border-b border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700 text-green-600 dark:text-green-400"><strong>Passed</strong></td></tr>
                      <tr><td class="p-3 border-b border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700">Block wins</td><td class="p-3 border-b border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700">74</td><td class="p-3 border-b border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700">26</td><td class="p-3 border-b border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700">0</td><td class="p-3 border-b border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700 text-red-600 dark:text-red-400"><strong>Blocked</strong></td></tr>
                      <tr><td class="p-3 border-b border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700">Below threshold</td><td class="p-3 border-b border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700">60</td><td class="p-3 border-b border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700">20</td><td class="p-3 border-b border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700">20</td><td class="p-3 border-b border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700 text-red-600 dark:text-red-400"><strong>Rejected</strong></td></tr>
                      <tr><td class="p-3">Under quorum</td><td class="p-3">6</td><td class="p-3">2</td><td class="p-3">0</td><td class="p-3 text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400"><strong>No quorum</strong></td></tr>
                    </tbody>
                  </table>
                </div>
                <p class="text-gray-800 dark:text-gray-200 leading-relaxed mt-6">Row 2 is the interesting case: 74% YES still fails because NO reached 26%. The block threshold protects minority positions from being steamrolled by any majority, however large.</p>
                <p class="mt-8 text-center md:text-left"><a href="#table-of-contents" class="text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-400 hover:underline font-medium">← Return to TOC</a></p>
              </div>
            </section>

            <!-- SECTION 7 -->
            <section id="bench" class="mb-20 scroll-mt-24">
              <h2 class="text-4xl font-black text-center md:text-left text-gray-800 dark:text-gray-100 mb-10 bg-gradient-to-r from-orange-500 to-pink-600 bg-clip-text text-transparent">7. The Objector's Bench</h2>
              <div class="prose prose-lg prose-orange dark:prose-invert max-w-none">
                <p class="text-gray-800 dark:text-gray-200 leading-relaxed">The <strong>Objector's Bench</strong> is a small group of eligible users who can pause any open vote by filing a public objection. It exists to give the community time to discuss a live proposal — not to override the vote.</p>
                <p class="text-gray-800 dark:text-gray-200 leading-relaxed mt-4">The bench's powers are deliberately narrow:</p>
                <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 text-gray-800 dark:text-gray-200">
                  <li><strong>Pause</strong> — 72 hours, once per bench member per proposal.</li>
                  <li><strong>Extend the vote deadline</strong> — the pause adds 72 hours to <code>vote_ends_at</code> so voters keep their full 5 days.</li>
                  <li><strong>Publish the reason</strong> — every objection carries a Markdown reason, publicly readable, and stays in the audit chain.</li>
                </ul>
                <p class="text-gray-800 dark:text-gray-200 leading-relaxed mt-6">What the bench <strong>cannot</strong> do:</p>
                <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 text-gray-800 dark:text-gray-200">
                  <li>Cannot pass a proposal.</li>
                  <li>Cannot block or veto a proposal.</li>
                  <li>Cannot alter the tally, the outcome, or the rules.</li>
                  <li>Cannot pause the same proposal twice.</li>
                </ul>
                <p class="text-gray-800 dark:text-gray-200 leading-relaxed mt-6">Bench members are selected by sortition (random draw) from the eligible user pool, with staggered term lengths so that no single cohort dominates. Every draw, every objection, and every expiry is on the audit chain.</p>
                <p class="mt-8 text-center md:text-left"><a href="#table-of-contents" class="text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-400 hover:underline font-medium">← Return to TOC</a></p>
              </div>
            </section>

            <!-- SECTION 8 -->
            <section id="reconsider" class="mb-20 scroll-mt-24">
              <h2 class="text-4xl font-black text-center md:text-left text-gray-800 dark:text-gray-100 mb-10 bg-gradient-to-r from-orange-500 to-pink-600 bg-clip-text text-transparent">8. The reconsider window</h2>
              <div class="prose prose-lg prose-orange dark:prose-invert max-w-none">
                <p class="text-gray-800 dark:text-gray-200 leading-relaxed">Every passed resolution stays <strong>open for reconsideration for 30 days</strong>. During that window, 10% of eligible users can sign a request to re-run the vote on the same proposal. If the threshold is reached, a second vote opens with the same rules, the same comment history, and the same audit trail.</p>
                <p class="text-gray-800 dark:text-gray-200 leading-relaxed mt-4">The second vote overrules the first:</p>
                <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 text-gray-800 dark:text-gray-200">
                  <li><strong>Second vote fails</strong> — the original resolution is reversed. If the proposal was Config, the config change is reverted. If it was Code, the merge SHA is marked reversed and the PR is expected to be reverted.</li>
                  <li><strong>Second vote passes</strong> — the original resolution stands. No further reconsider is possible on the same proposal.</li>
                </ul>
                <p class="text-gray-800 dark:text-gray-200 leading-relaxed mt-6">The reconsider mechanism is the safety valve. It means that passing a proposal is not the end of the story — if the community changes its mind within 30 days, it can reverse course without needing a new proposal.</p>
                <p class="mt-8 text-center md:text-left"><a href="#table-of-contents" class="text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-400 hover:underline font-medium">← Return to TOC</a></p>
              </div>
            </section>

            <!-- SECTION 9 -->
            <section id="execute" class="mb-20 scroll-mt-24">
              <h2 class="text-4xl font-black text-center md:text-left text-gray-800 dark:text-gray-100 mb-10 bg-gradient-to-r from-orange-500 to-pink-600 bg-clip-text text-transparent">9. Execution by kind</h2>
              <div class="prose prose-lg prose-orange dark:prose-invert max-w-none">
                <p class="text-gray-800 dark:text-gray-200 leading-relaxed">Once a vote passes, execution depends entirely on the kind:</p>

                <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-800 dark:text-gray-200 mt-8">Config — immediate</h3>
                <p class="text-gray-800 dark:text-gray-200 leading-relaxed">The config change applies the moment the vote closes. A one-line write to <code>rt_config</code>. No delay. Reversible via reconsider.</p>

                <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-800 dark:text-gray-200 mt-8">Meta — 72-hour delay</h3>
                <p class="text-gray-800 dark:text-gray-200 leading-relaxed">A Meta proposal queues a <code>pending_delay</code> execution scheduled 72 hours out. During those 72 hours the reconsider window is open. If 10% sign reconsider before the delay elapses, the execution is cancelled and a second vote opens. Otherwise the change applies and the reconsider window stays open for the remaining 27 days.</p>

                <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-800 dark:text-gray-200 mt-8">Code — human merge required</h3>
                <p class="text-gray-800 dark:text-gray-200 leading-relaxed">A Code proposal links to a pull request. When the vote passes, the proposal's state becomes <code>pending_merge</code>. <strong>Nothing auto-merges.</strong> A human maintainer reviews the PR, merges it, and the merge SHA is recorded on the audit chain. Without that human step, the code never lands — which is exactly how it should be.</p>

                <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-800 dark:text-gray-200 mt-8">Advisory — recorded only</h3>
                <p class="text-gray-800 dark:text-gray-200 leading-relaxed">An Advisory proposal changes nothing structural. The tally is recorded as a public signal. The audit chain entry is permanent. It's a way for the community to speak clearly without forcing an action.</p>

                <p class="mt-8 text-center md:text-left"><a href="#table-of-contents" class="text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-400 hover:underline font-medium">← Return to TOC</a></p>
              </div>
            </section>

            <!-- SECTION 10 -->
            <section id="audit" class="mb-20 scroll-mt-24">
              <h2 class="text-4xl font-black text-center md:text-left text-gray-800 dark:text-gray-100 mb-10 bg-gradient-to-r from-orange-500 to-pink-600 bg-clip-text text-transparent">10. The audit chain</h2>
              <div class="prose prose-lg prose-orange dark:prose-invert max-w-none">
                <p class="text-gray-800 dark:text-gray-200 leading-relaxed">Every governance action is recorded in a hash chain. Here's how it works in one sentence: each new entry contains a hash of the previous entry's hash plus the current payload. If any historic entry is ever modified, every subsequent entry's expected hash no longer matches, and the chain is visibly broken.</p>
                <p class="text-gray-800 dark:text-gray-200 leading-relaxed mt-4">Concretely:</p>
                <pre class="bg-gray-100 dark:bg-black/40 rounded-lg p-4 text-sm overflow-x-auto text-gray-800 dark:text-gray-200"><code>entry[n].this_hash = SHA256(entry[n-1].this_hash + "|" + type + "|" + payload)</code></pre>
                <p class="text-gray-800 dark:text-gray-200 leading-relaxed mt-4">Every governance table (proposals, votes, comments, objections, resolutions, executions) writes into the chain. <code>/api/rt/audit/verify</code> recomputes every hash from the genesis entry forward and reports intact or broken. <code>/api/rt/audit/head</code> returns the current chain head so external monitors can periodically snapshot it.</p>
                <p class="text-gray-800 dark:text-gray-200 leading-relaxed mt-6">The simulator demonstrates this visually. Open any scenario on <a href="/community/round-table/simulator/" class="text-orange-600 dark:text-orange-400 hover:underline">/community/round-table/simulator/</a>, scroll to the Audit Chain ticker, click the ⚡ tamper button on any block. That block turns red — and every block after it turns yellow, because the chain no longer connects. Click Verify and the alert reads <code>intact: false — broken at block #N</code>.</p>
                <p class="mt-8 text-center md:text-left"><a href="#table-of-contents" class="text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-400 hover:underline font-medium">← Return to TOC</a></p>
              </div>
            </section>

            <!-- SECTION 11 -->
            <section id="simulator" class="mb-20 scroll-mt-24">
              <h2 class="text-4xl font-black text-center md:text-left text-gray-800 dark:text-gray-100 mb-10 bg-gradient-to-r from-orange-500 to-pink-600 bg-clip-text text-transparent">11. The simulator</h2>
              <div class="prose prose-lg prose-orange dark:prose-invert max-w-none">
                <p class="text-gray-800 dark:text-gray-200 leading-relaxed">The simulator is a fully working demo of the governance engine, running in your browser, with no account required. It has three modes:</p>
                <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 text-gray-800 dark:text-gray-200">
                  <li><strong>Compact</strong> — a small embed on the homepage and the Round Table page. No autoplay. Click Play to run a scenario.</li>
                  <li><strong>Full</strong> — the dedicated page at <a href="/community/round-table/simulator/" class="text-orange-600 dark:text-orange-400 hover:underline">/community/round-table/simulator/</a>. Autoplay, scrubber, transcript, audit ticker, sandbox.</li>
                  <li><strong>Sandbox</strong> — a tab inside the full page. Sliders for electorate size, turnout, YES/NO split, and proposal kind. Move any slider and the outcome recomputes instantly, using the same rules engine the live server uses.</li>
                </ul>
                <p class="text-gray-800 dark:text-gray-200 leading-relaxed mt-6">Six scenarios ship by default, each teaching one rule:</p>
                <div class="not-prose overflow-x-auto mt-4">
                  <table class="w-full text-left border-collapse min-w-[500px] text-sm">
                    <thead>
                      <tr class="bg-gray-100 dark:bg-gray-800/80">
